# agents/ image — accepted vulnerability residuals (P0 security review, cmw-security-p0, 2026-08-12)
#
# Every CVE below is a Debian 12 (bookworm) base-OS package with NO fix available upstream. They
# cannot be cleared in place: the base is pinned to python:3.12-slim-bookworm because Playwright
# 1.49.0 does not support Debian 13 "trixie" (see agents/Dockerfile's header comment). A build-time
# `apt-get -y upgrade` is in the Dockerfile and will pull each fix automatically once Debian ships
# it; until then these are acknowledged, not ignored.
#
# Reachability: the agents container publishes NO host port — it is reachable only over the internal
# compose network, behind the `web` service. None of these packages parses untrusted, internet-origin
# input in this app's data flow. Classes are DoS / local / crafted-input, not remote pre-auth RCE.
#
# Re-evaluate on: any Playwright bump that unblocks a Debian-13 base, or when `trivy image` shows a
# FixedVersion for one of these (drop it from this file and rebuild).

# glib — integer underflow in gio/gdbusintrospection.c (DBus introspection XML). No DBus use here.
CVE-2026-58016

# perl — regex/compile + Archive::Tar/Storable issues. Perl is present only as system tooling; the
# app never runs perl on untrusted input.
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-8376

# sqlite3 — integer overflow via crafted DB. App uses Mongo, not local SQLite on untrusted files.
CVE-2025-7458

# libxml2 — DoS via crafted XML. No untrusted-XML parsing path in agents.
CVE-2026-6653

# openssh-client — use-after-free during host-key re-exchange. `ssh` is used only to push to a
# trusted, pinned GitHub host for the brain repo; not exposed to untrusted SSH servers.
CVE-2026-60002

# zlib — MiniZip heap overflow (CVE-2023-45853). Debian won't-fix for bookworm; not reached here.
CVE-2023-45853
